 "section_summary": "This section consists of the concluding portion of the Tokyo Embassy's monthly report for March 1938 (Report No. 138) with its appended tables of despatches and telegrams, followed by Despatch No. 3030 transmitting the monthly report for April 1938 (Report No. 139). The March report reviews the diplomatic resolution of the Alaskan salmon fishing dispute, debates over Japanese special military taxation of foreign nationals, military and aerial campaigns across China, Anglo-Japanese negotiations over Chinese customs, and domestic legislative measures such as the National Mobilization and Electric Power bills. Despatch No. 3030 and the April report chronicle American diplomatic protests regarding Japanese violations of foreign property in China, payment of the USS Panay indemnity, the arrest of American aviator Elwyn H. Gibbon, invocation of the London Naval Treaty escalator clause, the major engagement at Taierhchwang, Soviet-Japanese border and consular tensions, and Cabinet strains surrounding Premier Konoe.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "Continuation of the Embassy's monthly report on political, military, diplomatic, and economic developments in Japan and the Sino-Japanese conflict during March 1938.",
