   "start_page": 59,
   "summary": "Covers the conclusion of diplomatic exchanges concerning Alaskan salmon fisheries, Japanese insistence on levying special military taxes on foreign nationals, military operations in Shansi and Shantung, and the inauguration of the Renovation Government in Nanking. Also reviews British protests regarding postal censorship and the Shanghai customs, friction with the Soviet Union over consulates and fisheries, strengthening of relations with Germany and Italy following the Austrian Anschluss, and passage of major wartime legislation including the National Mobilization Law and the Electric Power Control Bill. Concludes with an extensive survey of Japanese economic, financial, and immigration policies, followed by complete lists of diplomatic despatches and telegrams forwarded to the Department during March 1938.",
   "title": "Report No. 138: Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of March, 1938",
   "to": "Department of State"
  },
  {
   "about": "Diplomatic despatch transmitting Report No. 139 on political, military, diplomatic, and economic conditions in Japan and occupied China during April 1938.",
