   "start_page": 96,
   "summary": "Ambassador Joseph C. Grew transmits Report No. 139 surveying Japanese political, military, and diplomatic conditions during April 1938. The report details vigorous American representations concerning military occupations of missionary property and trade discrimination in China, the receipt of indemnification for the sinking of the USS Panay, creation of the America-Japan Trust Fund, and the detention and release of American aviator Elwyn H. Gibbon. It further examines Anglo-American notification of intention to invoke the London Naval Treaty escalator clause, the major military battle at Taierhchwang and aerial combat over Hankow, British customs negotiations, acute Soviet-Japanese border and consular controversies, and Cabinet dissension surrounding Premier Konoe's health and China policy.",
   "title": "Despatch No. 3030: Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of April, 1938",
   "to": "Cordell Hull"
  }
 ],
